  "maxLevels": 7,
  "maxLevelsNote": "A consumer that lets a user add levels stops at 7. A scale that is already longer still draws by the rules",
  "alignment": "centered on its row. 10 is the capital height of the 14px title beside it",
  "placement": "On a card, the title row: title, #N, the meter, then the corner glyph (the desktop's globe, the phone's PR glyph). A card with no priority keeps no slot for it",
  "levelZero": "A card draws nothing at level 0. A list or picker that names every level (the Backlog pill, the Priorities popover, an automation's Priority condition) draws level 0 as every bar at opacity.none",
  "accessibility": "decorative: the element around the meter carries the level's name (\"Priority: High\")",
